# Egeria-baudot-subscription-processes
## Locate the types of subscriptions available for a digital product
##
## Each subscription type a product offers is a subscribing action process, built by the Product Manager's client
## (Jacquard uses it to build its catalogue; the Product Manager OMVS exposes it as the subscription-type requests in
## Egeria-api-product-manager.http).  Its qualified name is
##     ProvisioningActionProcess::<product name>::Create Subscription::<subscription type identifier>
## and its display name is "Create <subscription type> for <product name>", which is what the searches below match.
## The process carries the product, its asset, license, service level objective, product manager and notification
## type as action targets, so its remaining specification properties - the requester and the destination - are all
## a consumer has to supply.

@baseURL=https://localhost:7443
@viewServer=view-server

###
# =====================================================================================================================
# Manage the authentication token.  Run this request to create/refresh the token.

# @name Token (RequestBody)
POST {{baseURL}}/api/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId" : "peterprofile",
  "password" : "secret"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body); %}

###
# =====================================================================================================================
# Locate the types of subscriptions supported by a digital product
# https://egeria-project.org/concepts/digital-product


###
# @name find all subscription types in the catalog
# Every subscription option is a SubscribingActionProcess whose qualified name names the product and the type.
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/governance-officer/governance-definitions/by-search-string
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "SearchStringRequestBody",
  "metadataElementTypeName": "SubscribingActionProcess",
  "searchString": "::Create Subscription::",
  "graphQueryDepth": 0,
  "startsWith" : false,
  "endsWith" : false,
  "ignoreCase" : true,
  "startFrom" : 0,
  "pageSize": 0
}

###
# @name find Evaluation subscription governance action process
# Retrieve the list of governance definition metadata elements that contain the search string.
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/governance-officer/governance-definitions/by-search-string
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "SearchStringRequestBody",
  "metadataElementTypeName": "GovernanceActionProcess",
  "searchString": "Evaluation subscription for Valid Metadata Value Set: deployedImplementationType",
  "skipRelationships": ["SpecificationPropertyAssignment"],
  "maxMermaidNodeCount": 15,
  "startsWith" : false,
  "endsWith" : false,
  "ignoreCase" : true,
  "startFrom" : 0,
  "pageSize": 0
}

> {% client.global.set("deployedImplementationTypeEvaluationSubscriptionGUID", response.body.elements[0].elementHeader.guid); %}

###
# @name get the elements pre-loaded on the Evaluation subscription
# The action targets the process already carries: the product (digitalSubscriptionItem), its asset (sourceDataSet),
# its license (licenseType), its service level objective (serviceLevelObjective), its product manager
# (digitalProductOwner), its notification type (subscriptionManagerNotificationType) and the governance action types
# that provision and cancel a subscription.  The notification type is the one the Baudot Subscription Manager
# watches: for an evaluation subscription it permits a single notification, so the data is delivered once.
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/classification-explorer/elements/{{deployedImplementationTypeEvaluationSubscriptionGUID}}/by-relationship/TargetForGovernanceAction?startAtEnd=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "class" : "ResultsRequestBody",
    "includeOnlyRelationships" : ["TargetForGovernanceAction"]
}

###
# @name find Evaluation subscription specification
# Retrieve the list of governance definition metadata elements that contain the search string.
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/governance-officer/governance-definitions/by-search-string
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "SearchStringRequestBody",
  "metadataElementTypeName": "GovernanceActionProcess",
  "searchString": "Evaluation subscription for Valid Metadata Value Set: deployedImplementationType",
  "includeOnlyRelationships": ["SpecificationPropertyAssignment"],
  "maxMermaidNodeCount": 15,
  "startsWith" : false,
  "endsWith" : false,
  "ignoreCase" : true,
  "startFrom" : 0,
  "pageSize": 0
}

